//@version=6
indicator("Bullish Supply→Demand Flip Zones [v6.47 • Trading-Session Daily Resistance]", overlay = true, max_bars_back = 5000, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 200)

// Invisible output anchor for TradingView editor compatibility.
plot(na, title = "Output anchor", display = display.none)

// This indicator detects bullish demand-retest zones from supply flips and continuation bases:
//   1. A rejection pivot starts a live-safe supply formation. The formation extends forward until participation collapses
//      or price clearly disengages beneath the evolving supply band.
//      Its top is the highest high and its bottom is the highest close before the collapse bar.
//   2. A compact multi-bar rejection shelf may qualify collectively when no
//      single bar carries all of the body, volume, and trend evidence.
//   3. The seller-control structure must terminate at confirmed demand.
//   4. Supply may flip through a high-quality final break candle or a strong breakout impulse followed by acceptance.
//   5. After confirmation, all drawings stay hidden while retest logic remains active.
//   6. The full original supply structure appears when price first returns to the zone.
//   7. A zone touch or fresh re-entry controls visibility/state only; it never draws an S→D arrow by itself.
//   8. An S→D arrow requires either confirmed pivot support at the flipped zone or
//      a confirmed immediate post-breakout front-run defense.
//   9. A separate continuation-base path recognizes compact high-volume bullish shelves that launch higher.
//  10. Classic retests require two completed candles whose lows are above the
//      zone top before the later return.
//  11. A progressive-takeover path may use an earlier lower-edge defense
//      internally to validate a later breakout. It becomes a visible demand
//      indication only when that defense itself occurred after a prior cross.
//  12. A separate front-run path may recognize a near-zone rejection only after
//      the universal two-bar separation proof has already completed, and then
//      requires its low to remain preserved for the confirmation bars.
//  13. When multiple visible zones substantially overlap, an optional display
//      filter keeps only the broadest price area visible.
//  14. Timestamp-based candle-edge coordinates let zones begin on the true
//      origin bar without drawing the left border through its wick.
//  15. A supply retest that fails before confirmed S→D demand is removed entirely.
//      Only zones with confirmed demand preserve their successful history after a later break.
//  16. When drawing history reaches its limit, hidden and unconfirmed zones are
//      retired before confirmed S→D/BASE areas, preventing orphan arrows.
//  17. Broad-zone suppression requires the shaded rectangles to overlap in both
//      price and time; an unrelated zone from another session cannot hide one.
//  18. Every BASE/S→D area must survive three later bars after its evidence
//      becomes knowable live. An earlier breakdown removes the entire area.
//  19. The only active alert fires when live price first crosses above the high
//      of a recognized supply/BASE area, before the candle is confirmed.
//  20. A recognized hidden supply area becomes provisionally visible as soon as
//      live price first clears its top. Later lifecycle checks may still remove it.
//  21. A separate record-high trend path tracks the first-move auction from the
//      beginning of each exchange date. A new daily high with record trend-leg volume,
//      at least 50,000 shares, and a large upper wick becomes a candidate level.
//      After price clears that high, a later convergence bar may confirm demand
//      near the old high through EMA support or a strong lower wick.
//  22. EMA-band support uses the convergence candle's close inside the EMA 9–20
//      band, allowing a defensive wick beneath EMA 20. The volume benchmark
//      resets when each prior record-high candidate is crossed.
//  23. After a record-high breakout, intervening completed bars may undercut
//      the old high by no more than the configured percentage. A deeper low
//      cancels the pending HH→D setup.
//  24. Every demand indication must occur only after at least two earlier
//      completed candles traded fully above the zone with low > zone top.
//      The demand candle itself never counts toward this separation proof.
//  25. Supply-derived candidates are retired when a deep drawdown develops as
//      one-way hard selling: dominant lower closes, dominant bearish volume,
//      and no meaningful retracement of that decline. Continuation BASE zones
//      are unaffected.
//  26. A supply origin must own at least 60% of its actionable price zone:
//      no earlier comparison candle may overlap more than 40% of that zone.
//      Collective shelves compare only with bars before the complete shelf.
//      Record-high origins use the same upper-wick boundary that is plotted.
//  27. Daily EMA 20 and EMA 200 are plotted as overhead context. The first
//      approach from below that still closes below the EMA receives a visual
//      sale-warning label; the existing single early alert is unchanged.
//  28. Each daily EMA is drawn only while price is within the configured
//      percentage above or below it, preventing distant levels from compressing
//      the chart.
//  29. Daily EMA support defenses require a meaningful lower wick and recovery
//      above the EMA. The first confirmed close that loses accepted EMA support
//      is labeled as EMA FAILED.
//  30. A separate daily-resistance module retains live-safe pivot highs for 44
//      trading sessions when the red origin day has an upper wick, above-average
//      volume, and both price and volume exceed the neighboring daily candles.

// ─────────────────────── Inputs ─────────────────────────
groupSupply = "1. Hidden supply qualification"
pivotLeft = input.int(3, "Pivot bars left", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = groupSupply, display = display.none)
pivotRight = input.int(3, "Pivot bars right", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = groupSupply, display = display.none)
allowBearishSupplyCandle = input.bool(true, "Allow bearish rejection supply candle", group = groupSupply,
     tooltip = "Allows high-volume bearish rejection origins such as SDOT 2026-06-29 10:24. All wick, departure, trend, and volume filters still apply.", display = display.none)
minBearishOriginBodyAtr = input.float(0.45, "Bearish origin minimum body (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupply,
     tooltip = "Prevents small ordinary red candles from qualifying as bearish supply origins.", display = display.none)
minUpperWickAtr = input.float(0.10, "Minimum upper wick (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupply, display = display.none)
minBearishDepartureAtr = input.float(0.50, "Minimum bearish departure (ATR)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.05, group = groupSupply, display = display.none)
maxHiddenAge = input.int(750, "Maximum hidden-zone age (bars)", minval = 20, maxval = 5000, group = groupSupply, display = display.none)
maxHiddenCandidates = input.int(75, "Maximum hidden candidates", minval = 5, maxval = 250, group = groupSupply, display = display.none)
maximumPriorSupplyZoneOverlap = input.float(0.40, "Maximum prior overlap of supply zone", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupply,
     tooltip = "Each earlier comparison bar may cover at most this fraction of the origin's actionable supply zone. 0.40 requires the origin to own at least 60% of its zone. Collective shelves compare against bars before the shelf, not against their own member bars.", display = display.none)

groupSupplyStructure = "1a. Multi-bar supply structure"
expandSupplyStructure = input.bool(true, "Expand pivot into multi-bar supply structure", group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Walks backward through contiguous high-volume rejection bars that touched the pivot's supply band. The price band remains defined by the pivot.", display = display.none)
minSupplyStructureBars = input.int(3, "Minimum supply-structure bars", minval = 2, maxval = 10, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "The effective minimum is capped at Pivot bars left + 1 because the structure scan stays inside the confirmed pivot window.", display = display.none)
structureTouchBufferAtr = input.float(0.05, "Structure touch buffer (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure, display = display.none)
structureCloseBufferAtr = input.float(0.10, "Structure close buffer (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "A participating bar must touch the supply band and then close back at or below its proximal boundary, allowing this buffer.", display = display.none)
useForwardVolumeSupplyFormation = input.bool(true, "Extend supply until volume collapses", group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Starts at the confirmed supply pivot and extends forward through the active high-participation formation. The first collapse bar ends the scan but is not included in the zone.", display = display.none)
maxForwardSupplyFormationBars = input.int(10, "Maximum forward supply-formation bars", minval = 4, maxval = 30, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Safety cap including the original supply bar. If no dramatic collapse occurs, the formation freezes after this many bars.", display = display.none)
formationCollapsePreviousRatio = input.float(0.45, "Volume collapse vs previous bar", minval = 0.05, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "A bar may end the formation when its volume is at or below this fraction of the previous included bar's volume.", display = display.none)
formationCollapsePeakRatio = input.float(0.35, "Volume collapse vs formation peak", minval = 0.05, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Also detects gradual fading by comparing the current bar with the highest volume already included in the formation.", display = display.none)
formationCollapseRequiresBelowAverage = input.bool(true, "Collapse bar must be below volume average", group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Recommended. Prevents one merely quieter but still highly active bar from ending the supply formation.", display = display.none)
enableCollectiveSupplyShelves = input.bool(true, "Allow compact multi-bar supply shelves", group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Allows several compact rejection bars to qualify together when the final pivot bar narrowly misses the single-candle body, volume, or trend-location rules.", display = display.none)
collectiveSupplyBars = input.int(3, "Collective supply-shelf bars", minval = 3, maxval = 5, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "The compact shelf must end on the confirmed pivot high. Three bars captures SDOT 2026-06-03 07:10–07:12.", display = display.none)
collectiveMaxHighSpreadAtr = input.float(0.50, "Collective shelf maximum high spread (ATR)", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Keeps the bars clustered near one rejected price ceiling instead of treating an accelerating rally as supply.", display = display.none)
collectiveMaxCloseSpreadAtr = input.float(0.50, "Collective shelf maximum close spread (ATR)", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Requires closing prices to remain compact while supply is forming.", display = display.none)
collectiveMinAggregateRelativeVolume = input.float(1.00, "Collective shelf minimum aggregate relative volume", minval = 0.10, step = 0.10, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Compares the shelf's total volume with the sum of its per-bar volume averages.", display = display.none)
collectiveMinClosesAboveTrend = input.int(2, "Collective shelf closes above EMA/VWAP", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Minimum shelf bars that must close above EMA 9, EMA 20, and session VWAP.", display = display.none)
collectiveMinPriorAdvanceAtr = input.float(0.50, "Collective shelf minimum prior advance (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSupplyStructure,
     tooltip = "Requires price to advance into the shelf before the rejection develops.", display = display.none)

groupSellerLeg = "1b. Seller-control leg and demand termination"
requireSellerControlLeg = input.bool(true, "Require completed seller-control leg", group = groupSellerLeg,
     tooltip = "Requires supply to produce a multi-bar decline that ends at confirmed demand before it can flip to demand.", display = display.none)
demandPivotLeft = input.int(3, "Demand pivot bars left", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
demandPivotRight = input.int(3, "Demand pivot bars right", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
minSellerLegBars = input.int(3, "Minimum seller-leg bars", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
maxSellerLegBars = input.int(30, "Maximum seller-leg bars", minval = 3, maxval = 100, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
collectiveMaxSellerLegBars = input.int(40, "Multi-bar supply maximum seller-leg bars", minval = 3, maxval = 100, group = groupSellerLeg,
     tooltip = "Applies only when the supply origin spans multiple bars. It lets an extended seller-controlled decline reach its final confirmed demand without changing the 30-bar limit for single-bar supply.", display = display.none)
minSellerLegAtr = input.float(1.50, "Minimum supply-to-demand decline (ATR)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
minDemandLowerWickAtr = input.float(0.10, "Demand minimum lower wick (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
minDemandReactionAtr = input.float(0.75, "Minimum reaction from demand (ATR)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
minDemandRelativeVolume = input.float(0.80, "Demand/reaction minimum relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = groupSellerLeg,
     tooltip = "May qualify on the exact demand pivot or on a reaction candle before that pivot is confirmed.", display = display.none)
allowCompactSellerLeg = input.bool(true, "Allow compact high-volume seller leg", group = groupSellerLeg,
     tooltip = "Allows a 1-2 bar seller leg when the supply origin has exceptional volume and demand remains stable for the required right bars.", display = display.none)
compactMaxSellerLegBars = input.int(2, "Compact seller-leg maximum bars", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
compactDemandRightBars = input.int(2, "Compact demand confirmation bars", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = groupSellerLeg, display = display.none)
minCompactSupplyRelativeVolume = input.float(2.00, "Compact-leg supply minimum relative volume", minval = 1.0, step = 0.25, group = groupSellerLeg,
     tooltip = "Keeps compact pullbacks selective. SDOT 2026-07-17 07:09 measures approximately 3.87x average volume.", display = display.none)

groupContinuation = "1c. Bullish continuation-base zones"
enableContinuationBases = input.bool(true, "Detect bullish continuation bases", group = groupContinuation,
     tooltip = "Adds a separate live-safe path for compact, high-volume bullish shelves that immediately launch higher. It does not weaken the supply-flip rules.", display = display.none)
continuationMinBaseBars = input.int(3, "Minimum base bars", minval = 2, maxval = 8, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMaxBaseBars = input.int(5, "Maximum base bars", minval = 2, maxval = 10, group = groupContinuation,
     tooltip = "The detector tests the longest qualifying base first. Keep this at or above Minimum base bars.", display = display.none)
continuationZoneFloor = input.string("Lowest close", "Continuation-zone lower boundary",
     options = ["Lowest close", "Highest body low"], group = groupContinuation,
     tooltip = "Lowest close captures the full accepted shelf. Highest body low creates a narrower, more conservative zone.", display = display.none)
continuationMinAverageRelativeVolume = input.float(1.50, "Base minimum average relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMinBarRelativeVolume = input.float(0.80, "Each base bar minimum relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.10, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationHighVolumeThreshold = input.float(1.50, "High-volume base-bar threshold", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMinHighVolumeBars = input.int(2, "Minimum high-volume bars in base", minval = 1, maxval = 8, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMaxZoneWidthAtr = input.float(2.25, "Maximum continuation-zone width (ATR)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMaxCloseSpreadAtr = input.float(1.50, "Maximum base close spread (ATR)", minval = 0.10, step = 0.10, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMaxNetPullbackAtr = input.float(0.25, "Maximum first-to-last close pullback (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupContinuation,
     tooltip = "The last base close may sit slightly below the first close, but the shelf cannot materially roll over.", display = display.none)
continuationPriorImpulseLookback = input.int(5, "Prior impulse lookback bars", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMinPriorImpulseAtr = input.float(1.50, "Minimum prior impulse into base (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationBreakBufferAtr = input.float(0.05, "Continuation close-above-base buffer (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMinBreakBodyAtr = input.float(0.50, "Continuation breakout minimum body (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMinBreakRelativeVolume = input.float(1.20, "Continuation breakout minimum relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.10, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationMaxBreakUpperWickAtr = input.float(0.50, "Continuation breakout maximum upper wick (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.10, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)
continuationDuplicateWindowBars = input.int(10, "Duplicate suppression window (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = groupContinuation, display = display.none)

groupHardSelling = "1d. Hard-selling exclusion"
enableHardSellingExclusion = input.bool(true, "Exclude one-way hard-selling origins", group = groupHardSelling,
     tooltip = "Retires a supply-derived candidate when a deep decline is dominated by lower closes and bearish volume without a meaningful recovery. BASE continuation zones are not affected.", display = display.none)
hardSellingMinimumBars = input.int(8, "Minimum observed bars", minval = 3, maxval = 100, group = groupHardSelling,
     tooltip = "Prevents a candidate from being classified as hard selling from only a few candles.", display = display.none)
hardSellingMinimumDrawdownPercent = input.float(25.0, "Minimum drawdown from supply top (%)", minval = 1.0, maxval = 90.0, step = 1.0, group = groupHardSelling,
     tooltip = "Measures the running low beneath the supply-zone top.", display = display.none)
hardSellingMinimumLowerCloseFraction = input.float(0.65, "Minimum lower-close bar fraction", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = groupHardSelling,
     tooltip = "A lower-close bar closes beneath the preceding candle's close.", display = display.none)
hardSellingMinimumBearishVolumeShare = input.float(0.65, "Minimum bearish-volume share", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = groupHardSelling,
     tooltip = "Compares volume on bearish candles with volume on all directional candles.", display = display.none)
hardSellingMaximumRetracementPercent = input.float(30.0, "Maximum recovery of decline (%)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, group = groupHardSelling,
     tooltip = "Compares the largest closing recovery achieved during the decline with the full distance from the supply top to the current running low. A recovery reaching this threshold proves enough buyer participation to preserve the candidate.", display = display.none)

groupTrend = "2. Bullish-trend filters"
requireBullishTrend = input.bool(true, "Require bullish trend context", group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
fastEmaLength = input.int(9, "Fast EMA length", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
slowEmaLength = input.int(20, "Slow EMA length", minval = 3, maxval = 250, group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
trendSlopeBars = input.int(3, "Rising-average lookback", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
requireRisingEmas = input.bool(true, "Require EMA 9 and EMA 20 to be rising", group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
requireRisingVwap = input.bool(false, "Require VWAP to be rising", group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
requireSupplyVolume = input.bool(true, "Require supply volume above average", group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
minSupplyRelativeVolume = input.float(1.00, "Supply minimum relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
requireReactionAboveSlowEma = input.bool(true, "Require supply reaction to hold EMA 20", group = groupTrend,
     tooltip = "Keeps supply reactions that behave like pullbacks within a bullish trend.", display = display.none)
maxSupplyExtensionAtr = input.float(2.50, "Maximum supply extension above trend (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = groupTrend,
     tooltip = "Rejects exhaustion highs. Set to 0 to disable. The SDOT 07:09 setup needs approximately 2.35 ATR or more.", display = display.none)
maxBearishSupplyExtensionAtr = input.float(3.00, "Maximum bearish-origin extension (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = groupTrend,
     tooltip = "Bearish rejection origins may spike farther from trend before closing back down. SDOT 2026-06-29 10:24 measures approximately 2.76 ATR.", display = display.none)
useExtremeVolumeExtensionOverride = input.bool(true, "Allow extreme-volume extension override", group = groupTrend,
     tooltip = "Allows unusually active supply origins to exceed the normal extension limit. The seller-leg, breakout, and retest rules still apply.", display = display.none)
minExtremeSupplyRelativeVolume = input.float(3.00, "Extreme-volume minimum relative volume", minval = 1.0, step = 0.25, group = groupTrend, display = display.none)
maxExtremeSupplyExtensionAtr = input.float(4.50, "Extreme-volume maximum extension (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = groupTrend,
     tooltip = "SDOT 2026-07-01 09:30 measures approximately 3.79 ATR with approximately 9.7x average volume.", display = display.none)

groupFlip = "3. Flip confirmation"
requiredBreakCloses = input.int(2, "Consecutive closes required above supply", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = groupFlip,
     tooltip = "Two closes reject one-bar probes such as SDOT 10:46 and confirm the cleaner 10:49-10:50 break.", display = display.none)
allowImpulseThenAcceptance = input.bool(true, "Allow strong breakout impulse followed by acceptance", group = groupFlip,
     tooltip = "The first close above supply may provide the required bullish body, volume, and trend quality. A later consecutive close confirms acceptance even when that acceptance candle is neutral or bearish.", display = display.none)
breakBufferAtr = input.float(0.05, "Close above supply buffer (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupFlip, display = display.none)
minBreakBodyAtr = input.float(0.50, "Minimum bullish breakout body (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupFlip, display = display.none)
volumeAverageLength = input.int(20, "Volume average length", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = groupFlip, display = display.none)
requireBreakVolume = input.bool(true, "Require breakout volume above average", group = groupFlip, display = display.none)
minBreakRelativeVolume = input.float(1.20, "Breakout minimum relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = groupFlip, display = display.none)
requiredFullSeparationBars = input.int(2, "Fully-above bars required before demand", minval = 2, maxval = 10, group = groupFlip,
     tooltip = "Every demand indication requires at least this many earlier completed candles whose lows remained above the zone top. The demand candle itself is excluded.", display = display.none)
evaluateEvidenceIntrabar = input.bool(true, "Evaluate evidence before bar close", group = groupFlip,
     tooltip = "Required for the early alert. Signals are evaluated during the live candle and may disappear before it closes.", display = display.none)

groupProgressive = "3a. Progressive supply takeover"
enableProgressiveSupplyTakeover = input.bool(true, "Allow progressive supply takeover", group = groupProgressive,
     tooltip = "Uses a preserved lower-edge defense to validate later acceptance above supply. An S→D arrow is allowed only when the defense occurred after an earlier completed candle traded fully above the zone.", display = display.none)
progressiveBottomTestToleranceAtr = input.float(0.20, "Lower-edge test tolerance (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupProgressive,
     tooltip = "The demand candle may undercut the supply bottom by this ATR amount and must close back above the bottom.", display = display.none)
progressiveMaxBarsToAcceptance = input.int(20, "Maximum bars from demand to acceptance", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = groupProgressive,
     tooltip = "The takeover demand low must remain preserved until upper-edge acceptance completes.", display = display.none)
progressivePreservationToleranceTicks = input.int(1, "Demand-low preservation tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = groupProgressive,
     tooltip = "Allows this many minimum ticks beneath the candidate demand low before the progressive takeover is reset.", display = display.none)
progressiveMinAcceptanceRelativeVolume = input.float(1.20, "Upper-edge acceptance minimum relative volume", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = groupProgressive,
     tooltip = "The candle completing the consecutive closes above supply must reach this volume multiple. No bullish-body minimum is required for this path.", display = display.none)

groupImmediateFrontRun = "3b. Immediate front-run demand"
enableImmediateFrontRunDemand = input.bool(true, "Allow immediate front-run demand", group = groupImmediateFrontRun,
     tooltip = "After at least two earlier candles traded fully above supply, recognizes a near-zone defense whose low remains preserved during confirmation.", display = display.none)
immediateFrontRunProximityAtr = input.float(0.25, "Maximum distance above supply top (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupImmediateFrontRun,
     tooltip = "Applies only to this immediate post-breakout path. SDOT 2026-06-04 13:23 stopped approximately 0.215 ATR above the 8.2499 supply top.", display = display.none)
immediateFrontRunConfirmationBars = input.int(3, "Low-preservation confirmation bars", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = groupImmediateFrontRun,
     tooltip = "The front-run candle's low must remain preserved for this many completed bars before the historical S→D marker is drawn.", display = display.none)
immediateFrontRunPreservationTicks = input.int(1, "Low-preservation tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = groupImmediateFrontRun,
     tooltip = "Allows this many minimum ticks beneath the front-run low during confirmation.", display = display.none)

groupRecordHighTrend = "3c. Record-high trend continuation"
enableRecordHighTrendRetest = input.bool(true, "Allow record-high trend retests", group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "Tracks a same-day record high made on record trend-leg volume and a large upper wick, then converts that old high into demand after a later breakout and qualifying convergence.", display = display.none)
recordHighMinimumVolume = input.float(50000.0, "Minimum record-high bar volume", minval = 0.0, step = 5000.0, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "The origin bar must exceed this absolute volume and every earlier bar's volume in the current trend leg. The comparison resets when the preceding record-high candidate is crossed.", display = display.none)
recordHighMinimumUpperWickFraction = input.float(0.40, "Minimum origin upper wick / range", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "0.40 requires the upper wick to occupy at least 40% of the record-high candle's full range.", display = display.none)
recordHighMinimumRetestRatio = input.float(0.99, "Minimum retest low / old high", minval = 0.90, maxval = 1.00, step = 0.001, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "The convergence low may undercut the old record high by no more than this ratio. The default permits a 1% undercut.", display = display.none)
recordHighMaximumRetestRatio = input.float(1.01, "Maximum retest low / old high", minval = 1.00, maxval = 1.10, step = 0.001, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "Prevents a pullback far above the old high from being called a retest. The default permits a 1% front-run above the level.", display = display.none)
recordHighInterveningLowTolerancePercent = input.float(2.0, "Maximum intervening undercut (%)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "After the old high is crossed, an intervening bar cancels the pending HH→D setup only when its low falls more than this percentage beneath the old high.", display = display.none)
recordHighNearFastEmaAtr = input.float(0.15, "Near EMA 9 tolerance (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "A pullback may show buyer support when its low stops within this ATR distance of EMA 9.", display = display.none)
recordHighMinimumLowerWickToBody = input.float(0.50, "Retest lower wick / body", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.05, group = groupRecordHighTrend,
     tooltip = "0.50 means the convergence candle's lower wick must be at least 50% as large as its candle body when EMA support is absent.", display = display.none)

groupManagement = "4. Flipped-demand management"
invalidationMode = input.string("Close", "Invalidation method", options = ["Close", "Wick"], group = groupManagement, display = display.none)
invalidationBufferAtr = input.float(0.10, "Invalidation buffer (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupManagement,
     tooltip = "Allows a small close/wick penetration beyond the zone before declaring failure.", display = display.none)
minimumEvidenceSurvivalBars = input.int(3, "Minimum bars zone must survive after evidence", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = groupManagement,
     tooltip = "Counts from the live confirmation bar of BASE, S→D, progressive takeover, or immediate front-run evidence. If the zone invalidates before this many later bars complete, its entire area is removed.", display = display.none)
supplyRetestProximityAtr = input.float(0.10, "Supply retest proximity above zone (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = groupManagement,
     tooltip = "Allows buyers to front-run a flipped supply top by a small ATR distance. SDOT 2026-06-03 10:05 stopped at 6.32, only about 0.07 ATR above the 6.29 zone top.", display = display.none)
sendEarlyZoneBreakoutAlert = input.bool(true, "Send the single early zone-breakout alert", group = groupManagement,
     tooltip = "This is the indicator's only alert. Create it using 'Any alert() function call'. It triggers once during the live bar when price first crosses above a recognized zone high.", display = display.none)
maxHistoricalFlipStructures = input.int(200, "Maximum retained flip structures (history)", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = groupManagement,
     tooltip = "Retains older confirmed zones on long historical datasets. When full, hidden and unconfirmed zones are retired before confirmed S→D/BASE areas.", display = display.none)
maxHistoricalSupportMarkers = input.int(400, "Maximum retained S→D markers (history)", minval = 1, maxval = 400, group = groupManagement,
     tooltip = "Retains confirmed support arrows for older zones while staying within TradingView's label-object limit.", display = display.none)

groupDisplay = "5. Display"
activeFill = input.color(color.new(color.lime, 84), "Active demand fill", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
activeBorder = input.color(color.new(color.lime, 15), "Active demand border", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
invalidTextColor = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0), "Invalid-zone text/marker", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showSellerControlLeg = input.bool(true, "Show full supply/control structure after retest", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
sellerLegFill = input.color(color.new(color.red, 91), "Supply/control structure fill", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
sellerLegBorder = input.color(color.new(color.red, 55), "Supply/control structure border", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showContinuationBaseStructure = input.bool(true, "Show continuation-base structure after retest", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
continuationBaseFill = input.color(color.new(color.aqua, 90), "Continuation-base structure fill", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
continuationBaseBorder = input.color(color.new(color.aqua, 45), "Continuation-base structure border", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showFlipMarkers = input.bool(true, "Show zone-type arrows on retests", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showAdditionalSupplyRetests = input.bool(true, "Track every fresh S→D zone re-entry", group = groupDisplay,
     tooltip = "Tracks each later re-entry after price leaves the zone. Re-entry alone does not draw an arrow; only a confirmed demand pivot inside the zone does.", display = display.none)
showConfirmedSupplyFlipSupports = input.bool(true, "Mark confirmed S→D support arrows", group = groupDisplay,
     tooltip = "Marks qualified pivot supports and confirmed immediate front-run demand on their actual candles. Both paths retain their own wick, reaction, volume, and location requirements.", display = display.none)
showRetestMarkers = input.bool(true, "Show first-retest markers", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showLaterBreakMarkers = input.bool(true, "Show red marker when a retested zone later breaks", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showOnlyBroadestOverlappingZone = input.bool(true, "Show only broadest overlapping zone", group = groupDisplay,
     tooltip = "When visible S→D, progressive, immediate front-run, record-high trend, or BASE zones substantially overlap, hides the narrower price areas while preserving all detection, lifecycle, marker, and alert logic.", display = display.none)
broadZoneMinimumOverlap = input.float(0.75, "Minimum overlap of narrower zone", minval = 0.10, maxval = 1.00, step = 0.05, group = groupDisplay,
     tooltip = "The broader zone must cover at least this fraction of the narrower zone before the narrower area is hidden. The default 0.75 ignores small edge overlaps.", display = display.none)
zoneLeftPaddingBars = input.int(0, "Start visible area before origin (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = groupDisplay,
     tooltip = "Zero starts at the left edge of the true origin candle, keeping the border away from its wick. Higher values add whole-bar visual padding without changing detection.", display = display.none)
drawFromSupplyOrigin = input.bool(true, "Draw from original supply candle", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)
showTrendAverages = input.bool(false, "Show EMA 9, EMA 20, and VWAP", group = groupDisplay, display = display.none)

groupDailyEma = "6. Daily EMA levels and signals"
showDailyEmaLevels = input.bool(true, "Show daily EMA 20 and EMA 200", group = groupDailyEma, display = display.none)
dailyEmaMaximumDisplayDistancePercent = input.float(50.00, "Maximum EMA display distance from price (%)", minval = 1.00, maxval = 500.00, step = 1.00, group = groupDailyEma,
     tooltip = "Each daily EMA is hidden whenever the current bar's close is this percentage or more above or below that EMA.", display = display.none)
showDailyEmaSellWarnings = input.bool(true, "Show overhead daily-EMA sale warnings", group = groupDailyEma,
     tooltip = "Marks the first completed candle in each approach from below. A candle that closes above the EMA is treated as a breakout rather than a sale warning.", display = display.none)
showDailyEmaDefenseAndFailure = input.bool(true, "Show daily EMA defended and failed labels", group = groupDailyEma,
     tooltip = "DEFENDED requires prior acceptance above the EMA, a pullback into its proximity band, a meaningful lower wick, and a close back above. FAILED marks the first close below an EMA that was accepted above on the previous bar.", display = display.none)
dailyEmaDefenseMinimumLowerWickFraction = input.float(0.25, "EMA defense minimum lower wick / range", minval = 0.00, maxval = 1.00, step = 0.05, group = groupDailyEma, display = display.none)
dailyEmaWarningDistancePercent = input.float(1.00, "Warning distance below daily EMA (%)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 10.00, step = 0.05, group = groupDailyEma, display = display.none)
